AadhaarMethodVerifyTest
├── when every check holds
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the verifier is called
│   └── it should pass the decoded points and exactly the nine inputs
├── when the verifier accepts only a reversed b
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when input zero is another issuer key
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when input one is not the config nullifier
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when input seven is not the config nullifier seed
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when the config swaps nullifier and seed
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when input eight is not the signal of the digest
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when input eight is any other reduction of the digest
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when verify is asked about another digest
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when the verifier reverts
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the verifier reverts with the word true
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the verifier answers false
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the verifier returns nothing
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the verifier returns a short or a long answer
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the verifier returns a word other than true
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the proof is not 544 bytes
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the config has any length but three words
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when inputs three through six carry any values
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the freshness window is under an hour
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the freshness window is exactly an hour
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the signing time is exactly the window before the block
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the signing time is one second past the window
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when a stale proof matches every other input
│   └── it should answer the zero word
├── when the signing time is in the future
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the freshness window is the largest word
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the inputs match any key config and digest
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the method is paused and unpaused
│   └── it should answer the same before, during and after the pause
├── when the key admin rotates the key
│   └── it should accept the new key and refuse the old one
├── when the key admin rotates to any new key
│   └── it should accept the new key and refuse the old one
└── when the key admin rotates the key while the method is paused
    └── it should accept the new key and refuse the old one
